a return statement, but not all possible execution flows end in a return."

However, if the statements being extracted do not modify any variables,
and if there is only a single return statement, the extraction can be 
done by introducing a boolean return type:


public class RefactoredExample {

	public String foo(int a, int b){

		int x = 10;
		int y = 11;
		if (bar(x, y, a, b))
			return "aaa";
		int z = x + y;
		int w = x + z;
		y = w;
		return "ccc";
	}

	public boolean bar(int x, int y, int a, int b){
		if (x == a){
			return true;
		} 
		if (y == b){
			x = y;
		}
		return false;
	}

}

